---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import ProjectVisual from '../components/ProjectVisual.astro';
import PlaygroundScript from '../components/PlaygroundScript.astro';
import { profile, projects, services, principles } from '../content';
import { withBase } from '../urls';
const contactUrl = profile.contact.email ? `mailto:${profile.contact.email}` : profile.contact.github;
---
<Layout>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-topline mono"><span><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>SOFTWARE ENGINEER / BERLIN, DE</span><span>BUILDING IN THE OPEN</span></div>
    <h1 id="hero-title">{profile.hero.title[0]}<br /><span>{profile.hero.title[1]}</span></h1>
    <div class="hero-bottom"><div class="hero-intro"><p>{profile.intro}</p><a class="text-link" href={profile.github}>See what I’m building <Arrow external /></a></div><div class="visitor-paths"><a class="visitor-path path-team" href="#consulting"><span class="mono">FOR TEAMS</span><strong>Let’s sort out<br />the backend.</strong><span>Architecture, reliability & Java.</span><Arrow /></a><a class="visitor-path path-tools" href="#work"><span class="mono">FOR CURIOUS DEVELOPERS</span><strong>Find your next<br />useful little tool.</strong><span>Notes, releases & shortcuts.</span><Arrow /></a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-foot mono"><span>JAVA / SPRING BOOT / RELIABILITY / APIS</span><a href="#work">GOOD THINGS BELOW <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
  </section>
  <section id="work" class="work-section wrap" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / THE TOOLBOX</span><h2 id="work-title">One annoying thing.<br /><span>One useful tool.</span></h2></div><p>I like software with a clear reason to exist.<br />Here are three things I’ve put out into the world.</p></div>
    <div class="project-explorer"><div class="project-picker" id="project-picker" tabindex="-1" role="group" aria-label="Choose a project to preview" data-project-picker>{projects.map(project => <article class:list={['project-choice', `choice-${project.slug}`]}><div class="project-choice-top"><span class="mono">{project.number} / {project.kind}</span><button type="button" hidden data-project-button={project.slug} aria-pressed="false" aria-controls={`preview-${project.slug}`} aria-label={`Preview ${project.name}`}>Preview</button></div><h3><a href={withBase(`projects/${project.slug}/`)}>{project.name}</a></h3><p>{project.description}</p><div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href={withBase(`projects/${project.slug}/`)}>Explore the project <Arrow /></a><a href={project.source}>Source <Arrow external /></a></div></article>)}</div><div class="project-preview" id="project-preview-stage"><div class="preview-label mono"><span>LOOK INSIDE</span><span class="preview-desktop-label">REAL TOOLS. REAL INTERFACES.</span><a class="preview-back" href="#project-picker">Choose another tool ↑</a></div>{projects.map(project => <article id={`preview-${project.slug}`} class:list={['preview-panel', `preview-${project.slug}`]} data-project-panel={project.slug} data-project-name={project.name} aria-label={`${project.name} preview`} tabindex="-1"><div class="preview-copy"><span class="mono">{project.kind}</span><h3>{project.headline}</h3><p>{project.audience}</p></div><ProjectVisual slug={project.slug} /><div class="preview-footer"><div class="tags">{project.stack.map(tag => <span>{tag}</span>)}</div>{project.live ? <a class="text-link" href={project.live}>Try the app <Arrow external /></a> : <a class="text-link" href={withBase(`projects/${project.slug}/`)}>Read the project notes <Arrow /></a>}</div></article>)}<p class="sr-only" role="status" data-preview-status></p></div></div>
    <div class="work-end"><p>Open source means you can look under the hood, too.</p><a class="text-link" href={profile.github}>More on GitHub <Arrow external /></a></div>
  </section>
  <section id="consulting" class="consulting-section" aria-labelledby="consulting-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / BRING ME THE TRICKY PART</span><h2 id="consulting-title">What’s getting<br />in your way?</h2></div><p>I help teams design, review, and improve Java and Spring Boot systems. Start with the problem you’re actually trying to solve.</p></div><div class="challenge-workspace"><fieldset class="challenge-picker" data-enhanced-only hidden><legend>Choose a starting point</legend>{services.map((service, index) => <label><input type="radio" name="challenge" value={service.id} checked={index === 0} disabled data-challenge-choice /><span><span class="mono">0{index + 1}</span><strong>{service.choice}</strong><Arrow /></span></label>)}</fieldset><div class="challenge-static" data-static-only><h3>Where I can help</h3><p>Backend architecture, reliability and performance, Java and Spring Boot, and the technical choices for an early-stage product.</p></div><div class="challenge-results">{services.map((service, index) => <article class="challenge-panel" data-challenge-panel={service.id} data-title={service.title} data-prompt={service.prompt}><span class="mono">A POSSIBLE ENGAGEMENT / 0{index + 1}</span><h3>{service.title}</h3><p>{service.problem}</p><p class="engagement-result">{service.result}</p><ul>{service.outcomes.map(outcome => <li>{outcome}</li>)}</ul><a class="button" href="#contact">Let’s discuss this <Arrow /></a></article>)}<p class="sr-only" role="status" data-challenge-status></p></div></div><div class="process"><span class="mono">NO MYSTERY PROCESS</span><ol><li><span>01</span><p>Share the problem<br />and the relevant context.</p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Agree on scope,<br />deliverables, and timing.</p></li><li><span>03</span><p>Work through it together.<br />Leave with concrete next steps.</p></li></ol></div></div></section>
  <section class="approach-section wrap" aria-labelledby="approach-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / HOW I THINK ABOUT THE WORK</span><h2 id="approach-title">A few opinions.<br /><span>Held with evidence.</span></h2></div><p>I want to understand the problem before adding another piece of machinery.</p></div><div class="principles">{principles.map((principle, index) => <article><span class="mono">0{index + 1}</span><h3>{principle.title}</h3><p>{principle.text}</p></article>)}</div></section>
  <section id="about" class="about-section wrap" aria-labelledby="about-title"><div class="about-heading"><span class="eyebrow">04 / THE HUMAN PART</span><h2 id="about-title">Hi. I’m Volkan<span>.</span></h2><div class="about-sticker"><span class="mono">BASED IN</span><strong>Berlin.</strong><span class="mono">BUILDING USEFUL THINGS</span></div></div><div class="about-copy"><p>{profile.about}</p><p>The open-source side of my work is a good reminder to keep things practical: a note worth keeping, a release worth shipping, a shortcut that gets out of the way.</p><a class="text-link" href={profile.github}>My corner of GitHub <Arrow external /></a></div></section>
  <aside class="support-section wrap"><div><h2>Used it? Liked it? Help it along.</h2><p>If one of these tools earns a place in your day, you can support its continued development.</p></div><a class="text-link" href={profile.sponsors}>GitHub Sponsors <Arrow external /></a></aside>
  <section id="contact" class="contact-section" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><div class="wrap contact-layout"><div><span class="eyebrow">05 / YOUR NEXT MOVE</span><h2 id="contact-title">Tell me about<br /><span>the hard bit.</span></h2><p>I don’t need a perfect brief. A little context and a good question are a useful place to start.</p></div><div class="contact-card"><span class="mono" data-contact-context>START WITH YOUR PROJECT</span><p data-contact-guidance>What are you building, what’s getting in the way, and where could another engineering perspective help?</p><a class="button" href={contactUrl}>{profile.contact.email ? 'Send me an email' : 'Connect on GitHub'} <Arrow external /></a><p class="contact-note">{profile.contact.email ? 'Share the challenge and the context you think matters.' : 'GitHub is my temporary contact route. A direct email option will be added when it’s configured.'}</p></div></div></section>
  <PlaygroundScript />
</Layout>
